Changes to OCCT (V8_0_1) for the Open CAD Viewer. Applied by wasm/scripts/build-occt.sh.

- STEP: in a common datum (A-B, PMI RP 6.9.8) the modifiers of one datum_reference_element were
  added to the compartment's list and so also given to every later element: A Ⓜ-B read as
  A Ⓜ-B Ⓜ, and A Ⓜ-B Ⓜ gave B Ⓜ twice. Each element now gets the compartment's modifiers and
  its own. The datums of a compartment are read from its base, not from every entity it shares.
- STEP: nested common datums (an element whose base is another common_datum_list) are read,
  flattened into the compartment; each datum gets the modifiers of the elements it is nested in.
- STEP: a datum reference modifier with value whose length has no usable unit is left out; OCCT
  kept its type with the value 0, e.g. [Ø0]. A simple datum reference modifier not in the schema
  is dropped; it read as .ANY_CROSS_SECTION.
- STEP: a common datum element nested in itself (a malformed file) is read once.
- STEP: the axis system of a datum system (PMI RP Figure 64) is converted with the units of the
  representation it is given in; it was read unconverted, so inch files kept inch values.
- STEP, XCAF: situation features of [PT] [SL] [PL] (PMI RP Figure 66), linked to a datum reference
  by a shape_aspect_relationship named 'point/line/plane situation feature', are read into
  XCAFDimTolObjects_DatumObject::GetSituationFeatures and stored on the datum's label.
- XCAF: a datum object's modifier with value, its value and its position are initialised.
  XCAFDoc_Datum::GetObject sets them only when the label has them, so a datum without a modifier
  with value returned whatever was in memory.

